  "saint-charbel-prayer-for-a-miracle.html": {
   "The prayers below are excerpts from Day 1 of the Annaya monastery's published novena:": 1,
   "Paralyzed after a stroke, the Lebanese mother of twelve dreamed that Saint Charbel performed surgery on her in the night, and awoke healed on January 22 - the origin of the monthly 22nd pilgrimage (source: CNEWA's account and family interviews). She kept that pilgrimage monthly until her death in May 2025 (dated reports in Sources).": 1,
   "The prayer above is an excerpt from Day 1 of the Annaya monastery's published novena: 'Oh, Miraculous Saint Charbel, from whose immaculate body... come to my rescue and grant me from God the grace which I need.'": 1,
