  "saint-charbel-prayer-for-students.html": {
   "A prayer to Saint Charbel for students: exams, study, and finding your calling. Full text and short version.": 2,
   "Before the hermitage, there were the study years: the parish school in his mountain village, then philosophy and theology at Kfifan from 1853 to 1859. Students pray to Saint Charbel because he kept going - and finished.": 1,
   "The Student of Kfifan": 1,
   "Youssef Makhlouf studied at the parish school and tended the family's cows. He entered monastic life at twenty-three and later studied philosophy and theology at the monastery of Saints Cyprian and Justina at Kfifan from 1853 to 1859, under Saint Nimatullah al-Hardini. He was ordained in 1859. Every student who has ever had to keep going the hard way has a patron in him. The full education chapter is on the": 1,
   "\"Saint Charbel, student of Kfifan, you kept at the long work and finished. Pray for patience in my studies and courage to keep learning: give me a clear mind when I read, a steady memory when I review, and an honest heart when I am examined. When I am tired, lend me your perseverance. When I am anxious, lend me your silence. And when I do not know what my life is for, ask the Lord to show me the work I was made for - as He showed you, at Kfifan, at the altar, and on the mountain. Amen.\"": 1,
   "\"Saint Charbel, pray for patience in my studies and courage to keep learning. Clear my mind, calm my heart, and bring back what I have learned. Amen.\"": 1,
   "There is no historic text for students, but Saint Charbel is a natural patron: he studied at the parish school and completed six years of philosophy and theology at Kfifan from 1853 to 1859. This page offers an original prayer for study, exams, and vocation.": 1,
   "'Saint Charbel, pray for patience in my studies and courage to keep learning. Clear my mind, calm my heart, and bring back what I have learned. Amen.'": 1,
   "Saint Charbel is a beloved choice - he studied philosophy and theology at Kfifan under Saint Nimatullah al-Hardini - alongside the universal patrons of students such as Saint Thomas Aquinas.": 1
  }
 }
